Brown Sugar Berry Crumble Bars
  --Jenna, Butternut Bakery

Crumble:
1 1/2 c (195g) ap flour (or 1-to-1 gluten-free baking flour), spooned and leveled
1 1/4 c (125g) quick oats (use certified gluten free if needed)
3/4 c (150g) light brown sugar, packed
1/2 tsp baking powder
1/2 tsp kosher salt
3/4 c (168g) unsalted butter (regular or plant-based), melted 

Preheat the oven to 350F and grease an 8×8" baking pan. Line all sides with parchment paper and set aside. In a medium bowl, mix together the flour, oats, brown sugar, baking powder, and salt. Mix in the melted butter, taking time to ensure the mixture is evenly hydrated with no dry patches. It should turn very dense and thick. Press about 2/3 of the mix into the bottom of the baking pan. Bake for 10 min. Place the remaining crumble in the refrigerator. 

Filling:
1 c fresh blackberries, divided 
1 c fresh raspberries, divided
2 tbsp light brown sugar, packed
2 tbsp cornstarch
Zest of 1 lemon
2 tbsp lemon juice (for added tartness) or water
1 tsp vanilla
1/3 c (110g) strawberry preserves

In a bowl, add 3/4 c blackberries (115g), 3/4 c raspberries (105g), and brown sugar. Use a fork to give the berries a rough mash, making sure to mash each berry at least once. Then stir in the cornstarch, zest, lemon juice (or water), vanilla, and preserves. Pour the filling over the prebaked crust and scatter the remaining berries (1/4 c (30g) each) on top. Cover with the rest of the crumble and bake for 30-35 min. The surface should look slightly golden and the edges will be a tiny bit bubbly. Allow the bars to rest at room temperature for ~15 min, then transfer to the refrigerator cool completely, ~1 hr. Then lift out of the pan, slice, and enjoy! 

Notes: Frozen berries can be used for this recipe. Thaw the berries in a colander to drain any excess liquid. Then continue with the recipe as instructed.

